### Test dataset — demonstrates the auto-categorization pipeline.
### Each case sends controlled `categories` (= raw subjects) → the service
### applies WordBoundary matching + scoring → result is predictable.
### Categories: 1=unknown, 2=horreur, 3=romance, 4=aventure, 5=fantasy, 6=science-fiction

@apiBaseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@userId = 2

### 1. REGISTER — run once on a fresh DB (422 if account already exists, expected)
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{$dotenv DEMO_EMAIL}}",
  "username": "{{$dotenv DEMO_USERNAME}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv DEMO_PASSWORD}}",
  "confirmPassword": "{{$dotenv DEMO_PASSWORD}}"
}

###

### 2. LOGIN — sets HttpOnly cookies, auto-replayed on next requests
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{$dotenv DEMO_EMAIL}}",
  "password": "{{$dotenv DEMO_PASSWORD}}"
}

###

### 3. ME — current user info
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/user/{{userId}}

###


### CASE 1 — Scoring: 4 horror vs 1 romance → horreur wins
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/library/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "[DEMO] Case 1 - Scoring horror",
  "author": "Demo",
  "isbn": "DEMO-CASE-1",
  "coverUrl": "",
  "description": "",
  "publishingHouse": "Demo",
  "publishedAt": "2026-01-01",
  "categories": ["horror", "vampire", "ghost", "zombie", "love"]
}

### Verify CASE 1 → categoryName: "horreur"
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/isbn/DEMO-CASE-1

###


### CASE 2 — No match → falls back to "unknown" (id=1)
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/library/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "[DEMO] Case 2 - No keyword match",
  "author": "Demo",
  "isbn": "DEMO-CASE-2",
  "coverUrl": "",
  "description": "",
  "publishingHouse": "Demo",
  "publishedAt": "2026-01-01",
  "categories": ["cuisine", "philosophie", "essai"]
}

### Verify CASE 2 → categoryName: "unknown"
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/isbn/DEMO-CASE-2

###


### CASE 3 — Case-insensitive match (Postgres ~*)
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/library/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "[DEMO] Case 3 - Mixed casing",
  "author": "Demo",
  "isbn": "DEMO-CASE-3",
  "coverUrl": "",
  "description": "",
  "publishingHouse": "Demo",
  "publishedAt": "2026-01-01",
  "categories": ["HORROR", "Vampires", "GhOsT"]
}

### Verify CASE 3 → categoryName: "horreur"
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/isbn/DEMO-CASE-3

###


### CASE 4 — Pure single-category match
POST {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/library/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "[DEMO] Case 4 - Pure adventure",
  "author": "Demo",
  "isbn": "DEMO-CASE-4",
  "coverUrl": "",
  "description": "",
  "publishingHouse": "Demo",
  "publishedAt": "2026-01-01",
  "categories": ["adventure", "quest", "expedition"]
}

### Verify CASE 4 → categoryName: "aventure"
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/books/isbn/DEMO-CASE-4

###
